    "Across Siam, wedding venues range from compact family halls to larger destination-style properties, and the safa tying plan changes with the scale of the venue. Smaller, more intimate functions usually need a shorter, tighter schedule with the groom styled first and the rest of the group following quickly after. Larger multi-hall or multi-day venues need a longer plan, sometimes spanning more than one function in the same property, and we treat each function as its own booking within the same visit. Local venues in Siam are generally easy to access, which keeps setup time short, but properties further from the main area may need an earlier arrival buffer. We recommend sharing the venue name and rough guest count as early as possible, even before the date is fully locked, so we can flag any availability concerns during peak wedding weeks. If the celebration includes more than one ceremony — a haldi, a sangeet, the main wedding — let us know all the dates together so the Siam team can plan artist availability across the full run rather than one date at a time.",
